# Salvi-attack.lic
# Bigshot custom attack routine for Salvi (Cleric). Drop it into a bigshot
# hunting-commands list as a single command:
#
#   script Salvi-attack
#
# bigshot pauses itself, runs this once against the target it already has
# locked, then resumes to loot / wander / retarget -- so this does exactly ONE
# attack decision per call and returns; bigshot re-invokes it every pass while
# the target is still up. The moment the target dies -- at any point, including
# mid-hold after Condemn -- the script returns so bigshot resumes and fires its
# loot routine. Death is read off GameObj status (what bigshot itself uses), not
# a per-creature kill-message regex.
#
# Decision each pass:
#
#   mind at/near saturation:  don't cast at all -- flag bigshot to rest (see the
#                             overexertion guard below).
#
#   mana > MANA_FLOOR and     incant 301 in stance offensive, then Condemn (309)
#   301 actually affordable:  if 309 is affordable too -- an empowered evoke
#                             every EMPOWER_EVERY (10) plain casts *when there's
#                             mana for the pricier empowered cast*, a plain
#                             incant otherwise -- then drop to stance defensive
#                             and hold while the DoT ticks (bailing early if the
#                             target dies): CONDEMN_WAIT for a plain cast, the
#                             shorter EMPOWERED_CONDEMN_WAIT for an empowered one.
#
#   otherwise (low mana):     cast Symbol of Mana if it's known and off cooldown
#                             (cooldown-only check -- never spends deeds),
#                             otherwise wave a wand at the target (auto-draws a
#                             fresh wand from the fresh-wand container, retires a
#                             spent one to the dead-wand container; if there are
#                             no wands left it flags bigshot to rest).
#
# If a wound blocks spellcasting outright ("You can't think clearly enough to
# prepare a spell!" -- no roundtime at all), fires ;eherbs --spellcast once
# instead of retrying the dead cast, same as Salvi-duskattack.lic.
#
# Overexertion guard: casting once your head is at "must rest"/"saturated" (or
# within MIND_CEILING of it) risks nervous-system damage -- the cast goes through
# but you hurt yourself. If the mind is that full this skips the attack entirely,
# flags bigshot to rest, and exits. bigshot is paused while this runs, so its own
# rest threshold can't catch a mid-routine spike -- this has to self-police.

# --- knobs -------------------------------------------------------------------

# Attack while mana is strictly above this; fall back to Symbol of Mana / wands
# at or below it.
MANA_FLOOR = 10 unless defined?(MANA_FLOOR)

# Stop casting (rest instead) at or above this mind fullness, or as soon as the
# game itself says must-rest/saturated -- whichever comes first. Leaves headroom
# for the cast itself to nudge the mind up without tipping into the danger zone.
MIND_CEILING = 85 unless defined?(MIND_CEILING)

# Flat hold in stance defensive after Condemn goes off, letting the DoT work
# instead of instantly re-engaging. The empowered (evoke) cast lands harder and
# doesn't need the same long pause, so it gets its own shorter wait.
CONDEMN_WAIT           = 10 unless defined?(CONDEMN_WAIT)
EMPOWERED_CONDEMN_WAIT = 3  unless defined?(EMPOWERED_CONDEMN_WAIT)

# Condemn banks an empowered charge server-side every N normal casts. Rather than
# querying `spell` every cycle (slow, >2s), just tally casts locally: every
# EMPOWER_EVERY plain incants, the next Condemn is an evoke. The tally lives in a
# global so it survives this script being re-invoked each attack pass; it resets
# to 0 on a Lich restart, which at worst mistimes one evoke before it re-syncs.
EMPOWER_EVERY = 10 unless defined?(EMPOWER_EVERY)

# An empowered (prep + evoke) Condemn costs more mana than a plain incant --
# Spell[309].affordable? only knows the base cost, so require this multiple of it
# in hand before taking the empowered path. Short of that, cast a plain incant
# and keep the tally where it is (try the evoke again next pass).
EMPOWERED_MANA_MULT = 2.0 unless defined?(EMPOWERED_MANA_MULT)

# Wand config is read straight from bigshot's own loaded settings (UserVars.op)
# so it always tracks whatever profile is active -- Fresh/Dead wand container and
# the wand type(s) from the Attacking tab. The "wand" field is comma-separated
# and fallen through in order (shared with bigshot via $bigshot_wand) as each
# type runs out. Values here are only the fallback if the profile leaves them
# blank.
_op = (defined?(UserVars) && UserVars.op.is_a?(Hash)) ? UserVars.op : {}
_wands = _op["wand"].to_s.split(/,\s*/).map(&:strip).reject(&:empty?)
WAND_NOUNS = (_wands.empty? ? ["wand"] : _wands) unless defined?(WAND_NOUNS)
FRESH_WAND_CONTAINER = (_op["fresh_wand_container"].to_s.strip.empty? ? "greatcloak" : _op["fresh_wand_container"].to_s.strip) unless defined?(FRESH_WAND_CONTAINER)
DEAD_WAND_CONTAINER  = (_op["dead_wand_container"].to_s.strip.empty?  ? "bag"        : _op["dead_wand_container"].to_s.strip)  unless defined?(DEAD_WAND_CONTAINER)

# --- patterns --------------------------------------------------------------

# GS4 shows this when a wound (nerve/head wound, concussion, etc.) blocks
# spellcasting outright -- no roundtime at all, so a naive retry loop just
# burns the whole cast timeout every tick with nothing to show for it.
CANT_CAST_WOUNDED = /can't think clearly enough to prepare a spell/i unless defined?(CANT_CAST_WOUNDED)

# --- helpers --------------------------------------------------------------

# True when the mind is too full to keep casting without risking nerve damage --
# either the game has hit "must rest"/"saturated" (checkfried) or we're within
# MIND_CEILING of it.
def mind_too_full?
  checkfried || percentmind(MIND_CEILING)
end

# Tell bigshot to rest and stop here -- used when the mind is too full to cast.
def rest_for_mind
  echo "mind at #{percentmind}% (#{checkmind}) -- resting before I overexert."
  $bigshot_should_rest = true
  $rest_reason = "mind near saturation (overexertion risk)"
end

# Monster-agnostic death check: bigshot itself never text-matches kill messages
# (they vary per creature) -- it reads GameObj status, which Lich core keeps
# current from the room/combat XML. A dead creature reads "dead" while the corpse
# lingers, then "gone" once it decays or is looted.
def target_dead?(foe)
  return true if foe.nil?
  return true if foe.status.to_s =~ /dead|gone/
  !GameObj.targets.any? { |t| t.id.to_i == foe.id.to_i && t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }
end

# Sleeps up to `seconds`, but bails out early (checked ~4x/sec) the moment the
# target is dead -- so a kill during the post-Condemn hold ends the routine right
# away and hands control back to bigshot, which then loots.
def hold_unless_dead(seconds, foe)
  deadline = Time.now.to_f + seconds
  until Time.now.to_f >= deadline
    return if target_dead?(foe)
    sleep 0.25
  end
end

# Sends cast_cmd and collects every line through the roundtime message (a single
# dothistimeout match only sees the first matching line, not the whole result
# block). Stops early on CANT_CAST_WOUNDED, which never gets a roundtime line.
def cast_and_collect(cast_cmd)
  text_lines = []
  put cast_cmd
  end_time = Time.now.to_f + 5
  loop do
    line = get?
    if line.nil?
      sleep 0.1
    else
      text_lines << line
      break if line =~ /Roundtime: \d+ sec|Cast Roundtime \d+ Seconds?\.?/i || line =~ CANT_CAST_WOUNDED
    end
    break if Time.now.to_f >= end_time
  end
  text_lines.join(' ')
end

# True if there's enough mana in hand for the pricier empowered Condemn.
def empowered_309_affordable?
  base = Spell[309].mana_cost.to_i
  base <= 0 ? Spell[309].affordable? : checkmana >= (base * EMPOWERED_MANA_MULT).ceil
end

# Casts Condemn (309) at foe -- an empowered evoke once EMPOWER_EVERY plain
# incants have been logged AND there's mana for it (else a plain incant, tally
# untouched, try the evoke next pass), a plain incant otherwise -- and waits out
# its roundtime.
# @return [Boolean] true if the empowered (evoke) path was actually used.
def cast_condemn(foe)
  $salvi_condemn_casts ||= 0
  empowered = $salvi_condemn_casts >= EMPOWER_EVERY && empowered_309_affordable?

  if empowered
    fput "prep 309"
    waitcastrt?
    waitrt?
    fput "evoke ##{foe.id}"
    $salvi_condemn_casts = 0
  else
    fput "incant 309"
    # only advance the tally on a real plain cast, not on a deferred evoke
    $salvi_condemn_casts += 1 if $salvi_condemn_casts < EMPOWER_EVERY
  end
  waitcastrt?
  waitrt?
  empowered
end

# incant 301 in stance offensive, chain into Condemn, then hold defensive for
# CONDEMN_WAIT. Heals with ;eherbs --spellcast (touches only casting-blocking
# wounds) if a wound blocks the 301 cast outright.
def attack_sequence(foe)
  fput "release" if checkprep != "None"
  fput "stance offensive" if stance != "offensive"

  text = cast_and_collect("incant 301")
  if text =~ CANT_CAST_WOUNDED
    Script.run("eherbs", "--spellcast")
    fput "stance defensive"
    return
  end
  waitcastrt?
  waitrt?

  # 301 may have finished the target off -- don't Condemn a corpse or sit out
  # the DoT wait for nothing.
  if target_dead?(foe)
    fput "stance defensive"
    return
  end

  # 301 just nudged the mind up -- re-check before chaining Condemn so a spike
  # into the danger zone doesn't cost a nerve wound.
  if mind_too_full?
    fput "stance defensive"
    rest_for_mind
    return
  end

  # Don't chain Condemn unless it's genuinely affordable -- forcing a cast you
  # can't pay for is the overcast that hurts. If 301 spent us below it, just
  # hold and let the next pass (or a rest) sort the mana out.
  unless Spell[309].affordable?
    fput "stance defensive"
    return
  end

  empowered = cast_condemn(foe)

  fput "stance defensive"
  hold_unless_dead(empowered ? EMPOWERED_CONDEMN_WAIT : CONDEMN_WAIT, foe)
end

# The wand noun bigshot is currently on (shared $bigshot_wand index into the
# comma-separated list), advancing past any that can't be found until one works
# or the list is exhausted (nil).
def current_wand_noun
  $bigshot_wand ||= 0
  WAND_NOUNS[$bigshot_wand]
end

# One wand wave at foe. Draws the current wand type into hand from the fresh
# container first if neither hand holds a wand -- on "get what?" it advances
# $bigshot_wand to the next type in the list. If the wave doesn't produce a d100
# roll the wand is treated as spent and retired to the dead container. Out of
# wand types entirely -> flag bigshot to rest.
def wave_wand(foe)
  in_hand = [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand].compact.any? { |o| o.name.to_s =~ /\bwand\b/i }
  # a wand already in hand is waved as a generic "wand"; otherwise draw the
  # current type from the fresh container.
  noun = "wand"

  unless in_hand
    loop do
      noun = current_wand_noun
      if noun.nil?
        echo "Salvi-attack: out of mana and no wand types left -- resting."
        $bigshot_should_rest = true
        $rest_reason = "Out of mana, no wands"
        return
      end

      r = dothistimeout "get #{noun} from my #{FRESH_WAND_CONTAINER}", 3,
                        /You (?:remove|slip|slide|get|pull)|What were you referring to|I could not find|There (?:is|are) (?:no|nothing)/i
      break if r =~ /You (?:remove|slip|slide|get|pull)/i

      if r.nil?
        echo "Salvi-attack: timed out reaching for a #{noun}."
        return
      end
      # couldn't find this type -- move bigshot on to the next one
      $bigshot_wand += 1
    end
  end

  fput "stance offensive" if stance != "offensive"
  result = cast_and_collect("wave my #{noun} at ##{foe.id}")
  fput "stance defensive"

  # bigshot's own cmd_wand heuristic: no d100 roll seen -> the wand is dry.
  if result !~ /d100|You hurl/i
    fput "put my #{noun} in my #{DEAD_WAND_CONTAINER}"
  end
end

# --- main ----------------------------------------------------------------

foe = GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.id.to_i == XMLData.current_target_id.to_i } if XMLData.current_target_id
foe ||= GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ && t.name !~ /animated/ }

# nothing (live) to hit -- hand control straight back to bigshot, which loots
exit if target_dead?(foe)

fput "target ##{foe.id}" unless XMLData.current_target_id.to_i == foe.id.to_i

waitrt?
waitcastrt?

exit if target_dead?(foe)

if mind_too_full?
  # Head's too full to cast safely -- rest instead of risking a nerve wound.
  # Wands would be mind-free, but a saturated mind means it's time to rest
  # anyway, and resting recovers mana too.
  rest_for_mind
elsif checkmana > MANA_FLOOR && Spell[301].affordable?
  # Both gates: the MANA_FLOOR the routine is designed around, and 301's real
  # registered cost -- so we never open with a spell we can't actually pay for.
  attack_sequence(foe)
elsif Spell[9813].known? && !Effects::Cooldowns.active?("Symbol of Mana")
  # Off-cooldown check only -- never touches deeds (same check bigshot.lic and
  # Salvi-duskattack.lic use).
  fput "symbol of mana"
else
  wave_wand(foe)
end
